# Review routing.
#
# GitHub only honours an owner with write access to this repository. An
# unknown handle, or one with read access only, is silently ignored — the
# rule stops applying and nothing warns you. Verify access before adding
# anyone here.
#
# Every path below currently resolves to the same person, because the repo
# has one collaborator. The paths are still split by risk: when a second
# maintainer joins, the split is already correct and only the handles change.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                     @emmanuel-musau

# The security engine and the protocol text.
#
# A wrong derivation in `effects` means a user signs a transaction that does
# something other than what they were shown — the one failure this project
# exists to prevent. A silent edit to `spec/` breaks every implementation
# built against it. Neither should ever merge on a default review.
/spec/                @emmanuel-musau
/packages/effects/    @emmanuel-musau

# The gates themselves. Weakening CI or the lint rules should be a
# deliberate, reviewed change, not something that rides along inside an
# unrelated PR.
/.github/workflows/   @emmanuel-musau
/eslint.config.js     @emmanuel-musau
/turbo.json           @emmanuel-musau
